@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
title DELETE /api/workspace/v1/messenger/folder_items/{folder_item_uuid}
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "Controller is RestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\nFOLDER_ITEM + The container is tied up ." as DB
queue "It 's a transaction . outbox" as OUT
queue "Typed projected folder task" as TASK
participant "The worker pool ." as WORKER
database "The public events repository" as EVENT
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as DISP
participant "Signed client" as WS
Client -> API: DELETE the folder element
note right of API
  Removing the manual link
  The automatic membership only changes the worker projection .
  The source: active USER_STREAM_BINDING + It 's canonical . STREAM.is_archived = false
  All chats = All of them .; Personal = STREAM.private = true; Channels = STREAM.private = false
end note
API -> DB: BEGIN; Remove the element from the specified area
API -> OUT: I 'm going to add folder_item.deleted
API -> DB: COMMIT
API --> Client: 204 The answer is blank.
OUT -> TASK: immutable folder_projection(outbox_event_uuid, scope=user-folder)
TASK -> WORKER: claim user-folder(project,user,folder)\nlease + fencing
WORKER -> DB: Read the rest of it . normalized items + ready counts
group One . worker DB transaction
  WORKER -> DB: replace snapshot + counts + version/updated_at
  WORKER -> EVENT: ready folder_item.deleted {uuid} + effect guard
end
DISP -> EVENT: read/repeat/play
DISP -> WS: folder_item.deleted
@enduml
